1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Welcome to Archi-Flow — design cloud architectures with live simulation

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:06,580
Step 1 — Drag components from the palette onto the canvas

3
00:00:03,452 --> 00:00:05,952
Drag "Users" — represents your user base

4
00:00:06,865 --> 00:00:09,365
Add a Load Balancer to distribute traffic evenly

5
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:11,940
Drop two App Servers for horizontal scaling

6
00:00:14,604 --> 00:00:17,104
Add a Database for persistent storage

7
00:00:17,276 --> 00:00:19,776
And a Cache layer to reduce Database load

8
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:25,660
Step 2 — Connect components by dragging from port dots

9
00:00:22,462 --> 00:00:25,962
Hover a node to reveal its blue port dots, then drag to connect

10
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:27,760
Load Balancer splits traffic equally to both App Servers

11
00:00:29,455 --> 00:00:32,455
App Servers read from Cache first, then fall back to Database

12
00:00:37,408 --> 00:00:40,408
Architecture wired — 6 components, 6 connections

13
00:00:38,910 --> 00:00:42,910
Step 3 — Hit Run Sim to push live traffic through the design

14
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:46,920
Green nodes — system is healthy with 100 users at low latency

15
00:00:44,722 --> 00:00:48,722
Click any node to inspect live stats: load %, latency, P95, SLA

16
00:00:47,433 --> 00:00:50,933
Live metrics update in real-time as traffic flows through the node

17
00:00:50,075 --> 00:00:54,075
Click an edge to inspect traffic flow and set custom split percentages

18
00:00:52,931 --> 00:00:56,931
Set custom traffic split percentages per edge — or let Archi-Flow auto-balance

19
00:00:55,748 --> 00:00:59,248
The Overview minimap helps you navigate large architectures

20
00:00:57,604 --> 00:01:00,604
Collapse it with one click to reclaim canvas space

21
00:01:00,041 --> 00:01:02,541
Expand it again whenever you need it

22
00:01:02,799 --> 00:01:06,799
The Architecture Cockpit shows real-time cost, health, and node counts

23
00:01:04,457 --> 00:01:07,957
Minimize it to a compact ring indicator — maximizing your canvas space

24
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:08,982
Expand back to full cockpit for the complete breakdown

25
00:01:07,217 --> 00:01:11,217
Now ramp to 10,000 users — watch the bottlenecks appear

26
00:01:10,027 --> 00:01:14,027
App Servers turn red — overloaded! The bottleneck is clear

27
00:01:11,528 --> 00:01:15,028
The Suggestions panel auto-detects problems and proposes fixes

28
00:01:12,227 --> 00:01:16,227
One-click fixes: increase capacity, add replicas, or enable auto-scaling

29
00:01:14,228 --> 00:01:18,228
Enable auto-scaling on App Server 1 — watch replicas spin up automatically

30
00:01:19,192 --> 00:01:23,192
Replicas spin up — load distributes, nodes return to healthy green

31
00:01:21,707 --> 00:01:25,207
Export a PDF report, share a live link, or save to the cloud

32
00:01:25,682 --> 00:01:30,682
Archi-Flow — design, simulate, and present cloud architectures in minutes

